1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Nd4
4. Nxd4 { Takes the knight rather than the pawn on e5, which would run into ...Qg5. Black takes back and the exchange is equal in material. } 4... exd4
5. O-O { Castles first. Black's pawn on d4 cannot run away, and White is ahead in development, so the king comes to safety. } 5... c6
( 5... Bc5 6. Bxf7+ { Takes the pawn with check; after the king takes, Qh5+ wins the bishop on c5. } 6... Kxf7 7. Qh5+ )
6. c3 { Opens a file against the pawn on d4 and challenges it. } 6... Be7 7. d3 { Plan: take on d4 with the c-pawn, then play Nc3 and Bg5; the pawn on d4 will be weak. } *
